     A*
     A* The order header physical file. It is keyed on the order number,
     A* takes its field definitions from a field reference file where it
     A* can, and carries the validity checking the application relies on.
     A*
     A* Member: ORDHDR   Compilable: yes (CRTPF)
     A* Source: DDS for physical and logical files, IBM i 7.5.
     A* Retrieved: 2026-07-28
     A*
     A*
     A* File level. The reference file supplies field definitions to
     A* every specification that carries R in position 29.
     A                                      UNIQUE
     A                                      REF(ORDREF)
     A                                      LIFO
     A*
     A* The record format and its fields.
     A          R ORDREC                    TEXT('Order header')
     A                                      FORMAT(ORDFMT)
     A            ORDNBR         7P 0       TEXT('Order number')
     A                                      COLHDG('Order' 'number')
     A                                      CHECK(MF)
     A            ORDCUS         6P 0       TEXT('Customer number')
     A                                      COLHDG('Customer')
     A                                      RANGE(1 999999)
     A            ORDNAM    R               REFFLD(CUSNAM ORDREF)
     A                                      TEXT('Customer name')
     A            ORDDAT        10L         DATFMT(*ISO) TEXT('Order date')
     A            ORDTIM         8T         TIMFMT(*HMS) TEXT('Order time')
     A            ORDAMT        11P 2       TEXT('Order amount')
     A                                      EDTCDE(J)
     A            ORDSTS         1A         TEXT('Status')
     A                                      VALUES('O' 'S' 'C' 'X')
     A                                      DFT('O')
     A            ORDTAX         5P 3       TEXT('Tax rate') DFT(0)
     A            ORDNTE        50A         VARLEN TEXT('Free text note')
     A                                      ALWNULL
     A            ORDTS         26Z         TEXT('Written at')
     A*
     A* The key. A descending second key breaks ties by the most
     A* recent order first.
     A          K ORDNBR
     A          K ORDDAT                    DESCEND
